WEBVTT

NOTE Local synthetic narration draft: Microsoft System.Speech, stock en-CA voice. No external model or publication.

scene-01-cue-01
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.626
Evidence Board gives a research decision
room to be questioned.

scene-01-cue-02
00:00:03.626 --> 00:00:08.362
This fictional university is considering
longer library hours during exams.

scene-01-cue-03
00:00:08.362 --> 00:00:09.994
The current argument looks plausible,

scene-01-cue-04
00:00:09.994 --> 00:00:14.566
but do its sources actually justify
keeping the building open all night?

scene-02-cue-01
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.285
Seventy-two percent of voluntary survey
respondents wanted later hours.

scene-02-cue-02
00:00:20.285 --> 00:00:22.871
The question did not specify how late.

scene-02-cue-03
00:00:22.871 --> 00:00:27.068
Meanwhile, only eight percent of trial
entries occurred after midnight.

scene-02-cue-04
00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:30.871
That is a share of entries, not occupancy
or unmet demand.

scene-02-cue-05
00:00:30.871 --> 00:00:33.729
The original wording stays visible beside
the claim.

scene-03-cue-01
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.506
Ten structured WebMCP tools expose this
shared board to a compatible browser agent.

scene-03-cue-02
00:00:41.506 --> 00:00:45.396
Native registration and invocation have
been tested in Chromium.

scene-03-cue-03
00:00:45.396 --> 00:00:48.633
The setup panel reports actual
availability.

scene-03-cue-04
00:00:48.633 --> 00:00:53.939
Tools can inspect evidence and prepare
proposals, but none can approve a change.

scene-04-cue-01
00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:58.470
For this walkthrough, I’m using Run demo
rehearsal:

scene-04-cue-02
00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:04.440
a fixed six-call script through those same
handlers, with no model or API key.

scene-04-cue-03
00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:08.995
It proposes three changes and leaves every
one for human review.

scene-04-cue-04
00:01:08.995 --> 00:01:11.945
Nothing has entered the accepted record.

scene-05-cue-01
00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.920
The first proposal connects overlooked
counterevidence.

scene-05-cue-02
00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.040
The second makes the survey–usage tension
explicit.

scene-05-cue-03
00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.520
The third adds a question about exam weeks
versus ordinary weeks.

scene-05-cue-04
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.275
Each has its own rationale and proposed
result.

scene-05-cue-05
00:01:29.275 --> 00:01:33.485
I’ll keep the link and conflict, make the
explanation more careful,

scene-05-cue-06
00:01:33.485 --> 00:01:36.075
and leave the new question out.

scene-06-cue-01
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:42.036
Only when I click Apply selected does the
accepted board change.

scene-06-cue-02
00:01:42.036 --> 00:01:44.601
The unselected question is rejected.

scene-06-cue-03
00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:47.115
Invalid references or an outdated revision
are checked

scene-06-cue-04
00:01:47.115 --> 00:01:49.191
before a proposal or approval is
committed,

scene-06-cue-05
00:01:49.191 --> 00:01:53.241
so a failed operation cannot leave half a
change behind.

scene-07-cue-01
00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.480
The decision brief is a deterministic,
cited snapshot of the accepted board.

scene-07-cue-02
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.145
The accepted link and conflict are
included;

scene-07-cue-03
00:02:03.145 --> 00:02:06.480
the rejected research question is absent.

scene-07-cue-04
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.795
I can copy it or export Markdown.

scene-07-cue-05
00:02:09.795 --> 00:02:14.535
This is the evidence record we reviewed,
not a fresh AI answer.

scene-08-cue-01
00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:19.907
Activity identifies the rehearsal and
records tool inputs and results.

scene-08-cue-02
00:02:19.907 --> 00:02:22.988
Undo restores the previous accepted
content.

scene-08-cue-03
00:02:22.988 --> 00:02:26.799
A structured list and JSON backup keep the
same research usable

scene-08-cue-04
00:02:26.799 --> 00:02:30.307
even when native browser-agent support is
unavailable.

scene-09-cue-01
00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.795
Evidence Board makes a second perspective
inspectable.

scene-09-cue-02
00:02:34.795 --> 00:02:39.510
Follow the sources, review the changes,
and keep your judgement.

